{
  "_comment": "Copy to config.local.json and fill in. That file holds a live credential \u2014 keep it out of version control.",
  "flex_token": "PASTE_YOUR_FLEX_WEB_SERVICE_TOKEN",
  "nav_query_id": "PASTE_ACTIVITY_STATEMENT_QUERY_ID",
  "trades_query_id": "PASTE_TRADE_CONFIRMATION_QUERY_ID",
  "positions_query_id": "",
  "_how_to_get_these": [
    "IBKR Account Management -> Settings -> Account Reporting -> Flex Web Service",
    "Generate a token (this is flex_token).",
    "Then Settings -> Account Reporting -> Flex Queries, and create ONE",
    "Activity Statement query, period 'Last 365 Days', with these sections:",
    "  - Net Asset Value (NAV) in Base   the equity curve",
    "  - Change in NAV                   the NAV flow chart on Performance",
    "  - Cash Transactions               dividend income and the cost charts",
    "  - Trades                          per-trade commissions",
    "  - Open Positions                  gateway-free holdings (see below)",
    "Its Query ID is nav_query_id.",
    "",
    "Open Positions is what lets the dashboard serve holdings with IB Gateway",
    "off: EOD positions repriced by delayed quotes. Include the fields conid,",
    "symbol, listingExchange, currency, assetCategory, position, markPrice,",
    "positionValue, costBasisPrice, fifoPnlUnrealized, fxRateToBase,",
    "reportDate, and set Level of Detail to SUMMARY. Add the section to the",
    "Activity query above, or keep it as its own query and put that query's id",
    "in positions_query_id.",
    "",
    "Set that query's Period Detail to MONTHLY. Change in NAV then reports one",
    "element per month as well as the whole span, which is what the Monthly",
    "P&L toggle on Performance draws. Leave it off and everything else still",
    "works; only the P&L half of that toggle stands down, and backfill.py says",
    "so when it runs.",
    "",
    "trades_query_id is optional: set it only if you keep a separate Trade",
    "Confirmation query. With Trades in the Activity Statement above, leave it",
    "empty and the backfill reads trades from that one report instead \u2014 one",
    "Flex request rather than two.",
    "",
    "For Cash Transactions, include the types: Dividends, Payment In Lieu Of",
    "Dividends, Withholding Tax, Broker Interest Paid, Broker Interest",
    "Received, Other Fees, Deposits/Withdrawals.",
    "",
    "Then: /opt/anaconda3/bin/python3 adapter/backfill.py",
    "It prints which sections the statement actually carried, and names any",
    "that are still missing."
  ],
  "targets": {
    "_comment": "Optional. Target weights in percent per axis; keys must match the names the payload uses. Drives the Allocation drift bars.",
    "region": {},
    "sector": {},
    "currency": {}
  },
  "rules": {
    "_comment": "Optional. Thresholds for the Allocation rules panel.",
    "max_position_pct": 20,
    "cash_floor_pct": 5,
    "currency_band": {
      "HKD": 40
    }
  }
}
